  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Moscow wants a region it has not even captured. Here is what that demand looks like on the map."
  },
  {
   "id": "promise",
   "text": "Five stories, ranked by impact. Number three changes the most lines on the map."
  },
  {
   "id": "ch3",
   "pauseBefore": 0.4,
   "text": "Number three: talks on Ukraine could restart after November tenth. The obstacle is Donetsk. Russia demands the whole region, including the cities its troops have not taken, like Kramatorsk and Sloviansk. Russian forces have pushed toward Pokrovsk and Kostiantynivka for months. Luhansk is almost entirely under Russian control. Kyiv says a halt along the current front line is the most realistic path. Quick question: how much of Donetsk does Russia hold today? Take a guess. About three quarters, according to the Institute for the Study of the War."
  },
  {
   "id": "outlook",
   "pauseBefore": 0.4,
   "text": "So will talks start before mid November? Tell us in the comments: yes or no."
  }
 ],
